From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: emac0: DMA burst length of 32

With the default burst length of 8 words the TX DMA of the EMAC is no
faster than a 1 Gbit/s link, so the 4 KiB TX FIFO runs empty inside
frames that do not fit in it. Use bursts of 32 words, which lets
dwmac-sun8i allow MTUs up to 16358.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -1119,6 +1119,7 @@ emac0: ethernet@5020000 {
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_EMAC0>;
 			reset-names = "stmmaceth";
 			syscon = <&syscon>;
+			snps,pbl = <32>;
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			mdio0: mdio {
